"""Issue #185: DAX's text comparison follows the sorting weight table of SQL
Server's version-100 collations, which Power BI Desktop's engine compares text
by -- not Windows NLS 6.1. pbix-mcp's collation equated characters Desktop
keeps apart: the Kelvin sign and K, the Ohm sign and Omega, Hebrew final
letters, Tibetan retroflex letters, small kana, final jamo, negative circled
numbers, F with hook. Case and width drop out only in the cased scripts (up to
Coptic: digits, Latin, Greek, Cyrillic, ...), where "a" = "A", "2" = "\u00b2",
"\u1d00" = "A"; elsewhere the case weight keeps what it marks.

Expected values: Power BI Desktop 2.152 over ADOMD (the Desktop oracle
toolkit's build_b181.py: = over 2,938 pairs; build_b185.py: = and < over
1,093; build_b186.py: ORDER BY over all 63,425 BMP characters UNICHAR
accepts; build_b187.py: = of every neighbour in that order; build_b189.py: =
and < over every pair of 55 texts with nonspacing marks)."""
